{"author":{"id":"fb9734b7331903226ef3f5df545b960dd5ac64d18b49faee11e8b8e0bd561c91"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1783019168,"nonce":"+syKaiGlnrIvpz6gCL2Ka/CWmWM=","message":"CORRECTION to previous comment + actual root cause, confirmed by user observation (WDDM budget monitor) and probes:\n\nThe Krea run's weights are TORCHAO Float8Tensor, not quanto - runs 1-6 quantized via a qfloat8-\u003etorchao shim and the quantized cache (krea2_transformer_25f98aa...) serializes torchao tensors, which run 7 inherited (cache digest keys on the qtype STRING, so the shim output is invisible to it). The quanto pin fix from earlier stands on its own merits but was incidental to this crash (torchao was already routed to _pin_inner_tensors; rerun crashed identically).\n\nREAL root cause: layer_offloading_pinned_weight_gb=-1 auto-sized the pin budget to the whole model capped only by TOTAL RAM - but pinned (cudaHostAlloc) memory consumes OS-available RAM ~1:1 (measured; 'weights already in RAM so pinning is free' is false) AND commits against the WDDM shared GPU budget (~RAM/2, shared with every GPU process). Pinning 8.2-8.3 GiB at attach exhausted the ~28GB (12 dedicated + 16 shared) WDDM budget -\u003e next CUDA call of any size failed with raw cudaErrorMemoryAllocation, VRAM mostly free, no VRAM spike. Run 6 survived because pin_budget=0 kept everything pageable/evictable.\n\nFix shipped: MemoryManager._cap_auto_pin_budget caps auto budgets by min(total-8GiB, available-6GiB, total*0.25 as WDDM-shared proxy; env-tunable via AI_TOOLKIT_PINNED_WEIGHT_{RAM_FLOOR,AVAILABLE_FLOOR}_GIB / _WDDM_FRACTION) with a loud diagnostic when capped, applied in both attach() and attach_smart_training(). Plus a live floor guard in _move_params_to_cpu_and_pin (stops pinning when available \u003c floor regardless of budget). Tests: tests/test_pin_budget_caps.py (7). Expected on the 32GiB box: ~2 GiB pinned at attach, startup survives; raise via explicit layer_offloading_pinned_weight_gb if more pinning is wanted.\n\nStill open (separate ticket): native FP8 training gate regression - 'enabled (135 streamed linear layers)' on Jun 30 vs 'unavailable (0)' on Jul 2 with the SAME cache and env; gate predicates (Parameter/qdata/fp8/requires_grad) pass in isolated probes on both fresh and cache-deserialized pinned tensors, so cause unknown.","files":null}]}